{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDFeasibilityProxy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDFeasibilityProxy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Common","lean:module:QOU.HeckeAlgebra.Wedderburn"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDFeasibilityProxy.withinLengthBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDFeasibilityProxy.withinLengthBound","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PSDFeasibilityProxy.lean#L96-L106","doc":"The **length-bound proxy** for the canonical-T_w search: a candidate\nword is within the enumerator's search space only if `w.length ≤ L_max`\n(the R5-full SDP search bounds candidate length to `L_K_max ≤ 4`, per\n`binding-k-enumerator`'s parameter).\n\nNamed as a decidable predicate (§3b: naming, not asserting). The\nnecessity is the enumerator's search-space restriction — a definitional\nbound, not a derived theorem. The previous `(h : ¬P) : ¬P := h` was a\nself-assuming tautology that asserted nothing about braid words. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDFeasibilityProxy.evenPower_necessary_for_blockPosSemidef","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDFeasibilityProxy.evenPower_necessary_for_blockPosSemidef","kind":"axiom","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PSDFeasibilityProxy.lean#L77-L94","doc":"**Even-power proxy is necessary for block PSD.**\n\nIf `braidWordEval n w` has every Wedderburn block PSD, then\n`w.evenPower` (the decidable proxy on `BraidWord`) holds.\n\nContrapositive: a word violating `evenPower` cannot evaluate\nto a PSD-everywhere element.  This is the half of\n\"evenPower-iff-PSD\" that's actually true at the σ_k^{2m}\neigenvalue level.\n\nAxiomatised at the categorical-content level; concrete proof\nrequires the Hoefsmit-eigenvalue computation per block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.PSDFeasibilityProxy.braidWordEval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.PSDFeasibilityProxy.braidWordEval","kind":"opaque","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/PSDFeasibilityProxy.lean#L65-L75","doc":"**Abstract braid-word evaluation map** from a list of integer\ngenerator indices to a `WedderburnDecomposition n`.  Axiomatised\npending the Hoefsmit-based concrete construction.\n\nThe signature: takes a word `w : List Int` and a strand count\n`n`, returns the Wedderburn decomposition of the corresponding\nHecke-algebra element.  The map respects the Hecke and braid\nrelations (a downstream `axiom`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}